WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:04.400
♪♪

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.167
Narrator:
TABLE TENNIS IS MORE COMMONLY
KNOWN AS PING-PONG.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.901
FOLDING TABLE-TENNIS TABLES

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:12.767
ARE POPULAR IN HOMES
AND KEPT OUTDOORS

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:16.167
BECAUSE THEY CAN BE CLOSED UP
AND ROLLED OUT OF THE WAY.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:19.601
THESE TABLES CAN ALSO FOLD
DOWN ON JUST ONE SIDE,

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.334
ALLOWING FOR SOLO PLAY.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.567
[ UPBEAT TUNE PLAYS ]

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.100
THIS HIGH-END OUTDOOR
TABLE-TENNIS TABLE

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.601
HAS AN ALUMINUM BOTTOM

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.033
THAT PREVENTS THE TABLETOP,
CALLED THE PLATE,

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:36.767
FROM WARPING OR SPLITTING DUE
TO EXPANSION AND CONTRACTION.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:40.133
A PRESS STAMPS CUPS
INTO A SHEET OF ALUMINUM.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.734
THIS PATTERN CREATES
NEARLY EQUAL AREAS

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.634
BOTH IN CONTACT
AND OUT OF CONTACT

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.701
WITH THE REST
OF THE PLATE LAYERS,

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:48.868
PROVIDING FLEXIBILITY

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:51.767
TO WITHSTAND
TEMPERATURE-RELATED MOVEMENT.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:54.934
EACH TABLE NEEDS TWO EMBOSSED
ALUMINUM SHEETS,

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.067
ONE FOR EACH HALF OF THE PLATE.

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:58.767
♪♪

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.968
A TECHNICIAN ASSEMBLES FRAMES
FOR THE PLATE HALVES

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.534
OUT OF SQUARE EXTRUDED
ALUMINUM TUBES,

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:08.734
CUT TO THE LENGTHS AND WIDTHS
OF THE PLATE HALF PERIMETER.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:11.501
AN AUTOMATED MILLING MACHINE
MAKES MITER CUTS,

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:14.534
WHICH ALLOW THE TUBES
TO BE MADE INTO RECTANGLES.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:18.100
♪♪

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.300
THEN, THE TECHNICIAN
MOVES THE FRAMES

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.267
ONTO A ROTATING FIXTURE...

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:28.667
♪♪

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.767
...AND WELDS
THE CORNERS TOGETHER.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:39.701
♪♪

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:44.434
THE FRAMES ARE INSERTED
INTO A BRUSHING MACHINE.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.601
INSIDE, WIRE BRUSH ROLLERS

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.534
ALLOW THE ALUMINUM SURFACE
TO BECOME ROUGH.

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:52.300
THIS HELPS THE COMPONENTS
TO ADHERE TO ONE ANOTHER.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.968
♪♪

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:59.067
ANOTHER TECHNICIAN PLACES
THE EMBOSSED ALUMINUM SHEET

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.534
INTO A RECTANGULAR
ASSEMBLY JIG...

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:05.734
♪♪

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.000
...AND ADDS THE BRUSHED
ALUMINUM FRAME.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.734
♪♪

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:17.767
A CONVEYOR TRANSFERS THE JIG
TO THE NEXT STATION.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.067
THEN, THE JIG CONNECTS

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:21.834
WITH AN 8-MILLIMETER-THICK
SHEET OF PARTICLEBOARD,

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:24.300
MADE OF WOOD CHIPS AND GLUE.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.501
THE BOARD IS COATED
WITH A HEAT-ACTIVATED

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.467
ADHESIVE FILM ON BOTH SIDES.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:31.634
♪♪

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.067
AT THE NEXT STATION,

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:37.067
AN ALUMINUM SHEET IS PLACED
ON TOP OF THE PARTICLEBOARD.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.934
THIS STEP COMPLETES
THE PLATE COMPONENT ASSEMBLY.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:42.767
♪♪

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:46.167
NEXT, THE CONVEYOR LOADS
THE JIG INTO A PRESS.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:47.567
♪♪

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.667
ONCE 12 JIGS HAVE BEEN
LOADED ONTO THE PRESS,

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.467
IT HEATS TO 239° FAHRENHEIT

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:56.033
AND COMPRESSES THEM
FOR ABOUT 10 MINUTES.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.434
THIS PROCESS ACTIVATES
THE ADHESIVE

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:00.701
AND BONDS THE COMPONENTS
OF EACH PLATE

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.534
INTO A SINGLE UNIT,
ONE FRAMED PLATE HALF.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:05.901
♪♪

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:09.234
EACH PLATE HALF GOES THROUGH
AN AUTOMATED MILLING MACHINE.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:15.133
♪♪

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:19.467
THE MACHINE TRIMS ANY EXCESS
MATERIAL FROM ALL FOUR SIDES,

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:22.434
TO ENSURE THE TABLE
WON'T HAVE ANY SHARP EDGES.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:31.033
♪♪

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:37.534
♪♪

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:40.033
THE PLATE HALF GOES
THROUGH A PAINT MACHINE,

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.868
THEN INTO AN OVEN.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.868
THE PROCESS REPEATS,

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:48.067
APPLYING A SECOND COAT OF PAINT
AND A UV-RESISTANT CLEARCOAT.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.767
♪♪

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:53.100
A MACHINE APPLIES PAINT
THROUGH A SCREEN STENCIL,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.200
PRINTING THE LINES
THAT MARK THE BOUNDARIES

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.667
OF THE PLAYING SURFACE.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:04:00.834
♪♪

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:03.467
AFTER THE PAINT IS DRIED
IN AN OVEN,

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:07.767
A TEAM PLACES THE FINISHED
PLATE HALF IN A CARDBOARD BOX

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:11.133
AND ATTACHES FOLDING LEGS
TO THE BASE.

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:13.334
THE FACTORY
MILLS THE LEGS IN-HOUSE

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.133
OUT OF HIGH-TENSILE STEEL,

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.734
THEN FINISHES THEM
IN BAKED-ON PAINT.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.667
♪♪

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:22.234
THE NET, ALONG WITH
SEVERAL COMPONENTS,

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.167
ARE PACKED AND MADE IN-HOUSE,

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.767
WHICH THE CONSUMER LATER
ASSEMBLES TO THE TABLE.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.968
COMPONENTS INCLUDE
THE NET POSTS, SIDE PANELS,

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:34.567
WHEELS, WHEEL BRAKES,
AND THE BALL-RETURN BOX.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.901
FINALLY, THE PLATE HALF
IS TRANSFERRED

00:04:36.901 --> 00:04:41.467
TO AN AUTOMATED SYSTEM,
WHICH COMPLETES THE PACKAGING.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.167
MANY PING-PONG TABLES
ON THE MARKET

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:48.000
REQUIRE THE NET TO BE REMOVED
EVERY TIME YOU FOLD THE TABLE.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.801
THE DESIGN OF THIS TABLE ENABLES
THE NET TO REMAIN IN PLACE

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:53.868
WHETHER THE TABLE
IS FOLDED FOR STORAGE

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:58.367
OR HAS ONE OR BOTH SIDES
OPEN FOR PLAYING.

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:01.634
LESS SETUP TIME
MEANS MORE TIME TO PLAY.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.934
♪♪

